<title>NETHERLANDS: HBG upgrades profit forecast.</title>
<headline>HBG upgrades profit forecast.</headline>
<dateline>RIJSWIJK, Netherlands 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Construction firm Hollandsche Beton Groep NV said on Tuesday it expected a higher net result in the second half of 1996 than in the first half.</p>
<p>&quot;Based on the order book and the good geographic and sectoral spread, HBG expects a higher net result in the second half than in the first half, baring unforeseen circumstances,&quot; the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;The net annual result will therefore show a light rise relative to 1995 (104 million guilders),&quot; it added.  </p>
<p>In March of this year HBG had forecast that net profit for 1996 would be &quot;comparable&quot; to that of 1995.</p>
